    <div class="gp-sec" aria-label="The misdiagnosis"><div class="gp-wrap"><h2>I Blamed My Job. My Sleep. My Age. I Was Wrong On All Three.</h2><p>I did what most men do: nothing, and then everything. Slept more. Trained harder &mdash; which backfired, because recovery was the thing that was broken. Cut the drinking back. Bought the supplements that ended up in a cupboard, because who remembers six capsules across three timings?</p><p>Nothing moved, because none of it addressed the actual variable. The flatness, the softer body, the &ldquo;I'm fine&rdquo; evenings &mdash; these aren't personality changes. <mark>They're the symptoms of a hormone quietly stepping down 1% a year.</mark></p><figure class="gp-fig"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Testosterone decline curve" loading="lazy" width="820" height="820"><figcaption>It rarely looks dramatic. It looks like this &mdash; present, but not really there.</figcaption></figure></div>
